/F1 10.5 Tf (   6. Participation in another interventional trial within 30 days.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (   7. Any condition that, in the investigator's opinion, makes participation unsafe.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf () '
/F2 10.5 Tf (3. SCHEDULE OF ACTIVITIES) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Screening \(Day -14 to -1\): telephone screening call to verify eligibility questions; if) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (eligible, confirmation call to schedule the Baseline visit.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Baseline \(Day 0, clinic\): informed consent, vital signs, HbA1c, height and weight \(BMI\),) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (PHQ-9, EQ-5D-5L, MMAS-8, concomitant medications.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Weekly ePRO survey calls \(Days 7, 14, 21, 28, 35; window +/- 2 days\): symptoms, glucose) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (self-monitoring, medication adherence, adverse events.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Week 6 clinic visit \(Day 42, window +/- 3 days\): vital signs, weight, PHQ-9, EQ-5D-5L,) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (adverse event review.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Biweekly ePRO survey calls \(Days 56, 70; window +/- 3 days\): same content as weekly calls.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Week 12 clinic visit / End of Study \(Day 84, window +/- 4 days\): vital signs, HbA1c, weight,) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (PHQ-9, EQ-5D-5L, MMAS-8, end-of-study review.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf () '
/F2 10.5 Tf (4. ASSESSMENTS AND INSTRUMENTS) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (PHQ-9: 9-item depression severity questionnaire; total score 0-27. Item 9 \(thoughts of self-) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (harm\) must be escalated to a clinician the same day if scored 1 or higher.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (EQ-5D-5L: five-dimension health-related quality-of-life instrument plus a 0-100 visual) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (analogue scale.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (MMAS-8: 8-item Morisky Medication Adherence Scale; total score 0-8.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Home glucose: fasting self-measured blood glucose in mg/dL \(valid range 40-500 mg/dL\).) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Blood pressure: seated systolic/diastolic in mmHg after 5 minutes rest \(systolic valid range) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (70-250; diastolic 40-150\).) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Body weight in kilograms recorded to one decimal place.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (Dates are recorded in ISO 8601 format \(YYYY-MM-DD\). Missing responses are recorded as null,) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (never imputed.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf () '
/F2 10.5 Tf (5. SAFETY AND ADVERSE EVENT REPORTING) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (5.1 Definition. An adverse event \(AE\) is any untoward medical occurrence in a participant,) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (whether or not related to participation.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (5.2 Collection. At every ePRO survey call and clinic visit, participants are asked whether) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (they experienced any new or worsening symptoms, hospital or emergency visits, or medication) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (changes since the last contact. Verbatim participant description must be retained.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (5.3 Serious AEs \(SAEs\). Any death, hospitalization, life-threatening event, or significant) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (disability must be reported by the site to the sponsor within 24 hours of awareness.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (5.4 Escalation rules for automated calls. The voice agent must flag a call for human review) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (when a participant reports: chest pain, fainting, glucose below 54 mg/dL or above 400 mg/dL,) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (systolic blood pressure above 180 mmHg, any thought of self-harm, hospitalization, or) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (unclear/contradictory answers to an eligibility question. A study coordinator reviews) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (flagged calls the same business day.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (5.5 Withdrawal. Participants may withdraw at any time without penalty. Withdrawal status is) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (recorded with the date and stated reason, if given.) '
/F1 10.5 Tf () '
/F2 10.5 Tf (6. DATA MANAGEMENT AND REGULATORY NOTES) '
/F1 10.5 Tf (All data are captured in an electronic data capture \(EDC\) system with audit trail. Every) '
ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 266.0 30 Td (Page 2 of 3) Tj ET
